    "bio": "a Representative from Washington; born in Detroit Lakes, Becker County, Minn., August 29, 1950; graduated, Kent Meridian High School, Kent, Wash., 1968; A.A., Concordia Lutheran College, Portland, Oreg., 1970; United States Air Force Reserve, 1971-1976; United States Air Force, 1976; police officer, King County, Wash., 1972-1997; sheriff, King County, Wash., 1997- 2004; elected as a Republican to the One Hundred Ninth and to the six succeeding Congresses (January 3, 2005-January 3, 2019); was not a candidate for reelection to the One Hundred Sixteenth Congress in 2018; unsuccessful candidate for Governor of Washington in 2024.",
